    "reason": "The English lemma 'mate' (concept-core-mate, general, daily_life) primarily refers to a friend or companion. While '大将' (taishō) does have a sense meaning 'mate' or 'old chap' (Sense 2), it is also commonly used to mean 'general', 'admiral', 'head', or 'chief' (Sense 0, Sense 1). This makes '大将' semantically broader than the core 'mate' concept. Furthermore, '大将' is not the most natural or general term a learner would expect for 'mate' (friend/companion); more common equivalents like '友達' (tomodachi), '仲間' (nakama), or '相棒' (aibō) exist.",
